# SAST scope for this repository (Semgrep CE, via the semgrep-scan orb).
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: tests/, testprojects/ and every other test tree.
# Semgrep's built-in ignore list drops test code, and test code here runs in CI
# with real repository credentials, so it stays in scope. The set below is
# pinned by the disposition-check job (semgrepignore-baseline): adding an entry
# fails the build until the baseline is updated in a reviewed change.

# Dependencies, VCS metadata and build output: not first-party code.
.git/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
target/
dist/
build/

# Helm chart TEMPLATE, not a chart: `version: {VERSION}` and `{SERVICE_NAME}`
# are placeholders servicemaker substitutes when it generates a service chart,
# so these files are not parseable YAML and semgrep reports a syntax error for
# each one. Excluded because they can never be analysed, not to hide findings.
charts/templates/

# Semgrep's bash parser fails on the `${ARCHIVE_FILE:-<not set>}` default value
# on line 13 (a partial parse, so the rest of the file is analysed with no
# error reported). Excluded rather than left as a permanent strict-mode failure;
# revisit when semgrep's bash parser handles the construct.
baseimages/scripts/entrypoint.sh
